is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: leaf_router_0_0
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: BGP export policy on leaf_router_0_0. The router is not advertising its local subnet 10.0.0.0/24 into the fabric.

Mechanism: With eBGP sessions Established, the spines learn and retain routes only for prefixes that leaves actively advertise. leaf_router_0_1 correctly advertises 10.0.1.0/24, so both spines have that route. leaf_router_0_0 is missing any “network” or redistribution for 10.0.0.0/24, so the spines (and the other leaf) never learn it. Pings from pc_0_0 to pc_0_1 go out via the learned 10.0.1.0/24 route, but the return path fails at the spines due to lack of 10.0.0.0/24, causing end-to-end failure while each host can still reach its local gateway.

Localization: On leaf_router_0_0, running-config shows no BGP address-family network statement (router bgp 65200 has only neighbor lines, no network or redistribute). The route 10.0.0.0/24 is present locally as connected (C>* 10.0.0.0/24 is directly connected, eth2). On both spines, show ip route displays only BGP 10.0.1.0/24 and no 10.0.0.0/24, confirming non-propagation.

Root cause: Misconfiguration on leaf_router_0_0—its BGP process is not configured to advertise 10.0.0.0/24.

Corrective fix: On leaf_router_0_0, add under router bgp 65200:
 address-family ipv4 unicast
  network 10.0.0.0/24
 exit-address-family
Alternatively, use “redistribute connected” with an appropriate route-map to limit scope. Commit and verify spines now show BGP 10.0.0.0/24 and end-to-end ping succeeds. 
=== END ===